# ra1_checks.py seed=20261016 python 3.11.15 numpy 2.4.6

== A. Lemma 3.2 with eps > eps*: |e| = eps* = 1, eps = 2, Delta = 3 = eps + eps* (claimed coarse regime)
   simulated: Pr[prove] = 0.0000, Pr[refute] = 0.0000, Pr[silent] = 1.0000
   Lemma 3.2 coarse-regime formula: Pr[silent] = 2 eps/Delta = 1.3333  (> 1: impossible)
   the general formulas give prove = (1-(eps+max(|e|,eps))/Delta)^+ = 0.0000, refute = 0, silent = 1
   => the coarse regime must be Delta >= eps + max(eps, eps*), i.e. Delta >= 2 eps when eps > eps*.

