== D. Q/rand threshold thr(p) = 1/2 + H2(p)/(2 p gamma), gamma = log2(360) (Delta = 60', full circle)
   p = 1e-02: threshold 0.976
   p = 5e-03: threshold 1.035
   p = 1e-03: threshold 1.172
   p = 1e-04: threshold 1.367
   p = 1e-06: threshold 1.759
   p = 1e-09: threshold 2.345
   p = 1e-12: threshold 2.932
   p = 1e-15: threshold 3.519
   the threshold grows like log2(e/p)/(2 gamma) as p -> 0; it does not 'stay near 1'.

== E. Setting S3 with times i.i.d. uniform on a grid of N days (repeats), sinusoidal error eps* = 1',
   Delta = 60', R = 21600', gamma = log2(R/Delta), lambda = 1, pi_c = log2(N) + 2 (as in section 3.6)
   Prop 3.3 rates (distinct times): m_P(Q/det) = 0.2397, m_H(Q) = 0.2831, m_H(R) = 0.0295, m_0 = 8.4919
          n    K_n/n   P(Q/det)/n       H(Q)/n       H(R)/n  P refuted t
       1000   0.8990       0.3954       0.2632       0.0367           16
       3000   0.7320       0.3738       0.3142       0.0358           41
      10000   0.3947       0.4950       0.3201       0.0325          115
      30000   0.1461       0.8273       0.3006       0.0294          310
     100000   0.0438       1.9561       0.2837       0.0256          917
     200000   0.0219       3.2274       0.2825       0.0223         1592
   With repeated times the patched law withdraws the law at every refuted time, so all later data there
   are exceptions: its per-datum cost rises towards gamma*Pr[t eventually refuted], while code R's honest
   cost per datum falls (cells at one time intersect).  Prop 3.3's rates hold only for distinct times.

== F. Prop 7.1(d): H^{eps_min} does not imply the common consequence T_0 \/ T_N (W = 1, P = J R)
   Ra = ['3/5', '4/5'], Aa = ['74/125', '403/500'], eps_min(1)^2 = 1/10000
   x_1 := Ra + eta P a / 2 = ['149/250', '803/1000']: |x_1 - Ra|^2 = 1/40000 <= eps_min^2: True; x_1 = Ra: False; x_1 = Aa: False
   so (x_0, x_1) = (a, x_1) is a real model of H^{eps_min}_1 and of neither T_0^1 nor T_N^1; the strongest
   common consequence of T_0^1 and T_N^1 is their disjunction, strictly stronger than H^{eps_min}_1.

